{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this admission. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been having sharp pain in my upper abdomen, constant nausea, and dizziness when I stand. I threw up once—greenish, not bloody. I haven’t eaten much—just a little pudding yesterday morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds similar to your past episodes. You’ve had several hospitalizations recently for partial bowel obstructions, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, five in the last three months. I was just discharged two days ago on a full liquid diet, but the pain and nausea came back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. We reviewed your CT scan from today. It shows no major change from the one five days ago. There’s still a piece of old tubing in your small bowel that might be causing irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The tubing from my old GJ tube? I thought that might be the issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. The scan shows new wall thickening around that area, which could be contributing to the partial obstruction. But there’s no sign of a complete blockage or free air, so surgery isn’t needed right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s the plan? I’m so tired of being sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue with bowel rest—no food by mouth for now. You’ll get fluids through an IV, and we’ll manage your nausea with Phenergan and your pain with your usual morphine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my G-tube? It’s been draining a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep it to gravity drainage, not suction. It’s helping decompress your stomach. Also, we’ve scheduled to replace the G-tube tomorrow—it was already planned, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s been leaking a bit. I’m glad we’re doing that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2181-12-05 18:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. The procedure is low-risk and will be done under fluoroscopy to make sure the new tube is placed correctly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2181-12-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2181-12-06 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous, but the pain is a little less. I’m really weak and dizzy when I try to sit up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2181-12-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure was low this morning—75 over 51 when you stood. That explains the dizziness. We’re giving you more IV fluids to help with dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2181-12-06 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been dizzy for months, but it’s worse now. Is that from the bowel issue?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2181-12-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. Dehydration and not eating are making it worse. We’ll keep monitoring it. Your labs show your hemoglobin is a bit low, but stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2181-12-06 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my INR? I’m on Coumadin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2181-12-06 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your PTT was high on admission—150—but it’s coming down. We’ll check it again soon. No bleeding, so we’re continuing your warfarin at the same dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2181-12-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to take you for your G-tube replacement. Any questions before we go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2181-12-07 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt? How long does it take?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2181-12-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get some sedation, so you’ll be relaxed. It usually takes about 30 minutes. They’ll confirm the placement with contrast to make sure it’s in the stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2181-12-07 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure went perfectly. The new G-tube is in place, and the contrast confirmed it’s in the stomach. You did great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2181-12-07 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel a little pressure, but no pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2181-12-07 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. We’ll keep it clamped for a bit, then start with gravity drainage. Once you’re stable, we’ll try advancing your diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2181-12-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your nausea has improved, and the G-tube output has decreased. We’re going to try starting you on clear liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2181-12-08 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have some broth or apple juice?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2181-12-08 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with small amounts. We’ll also clamp the G-tube for 45 minutes after each intake to see how you tolerate it without drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2181-12-08 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with the liquids. No vomiting, and the clamp test was successful. We’re going to advance to full liquids—like yogurt, pudding, and Ensure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2181-12-08 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds good. I’m hungry. But I’m worried about the Ensure—won’t that affect my phosphate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2181-12-08 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. Your phosphate was high this morning—6.3. You’ll need to take two TUMS with each bottle of Ensure to bind the phosphate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2181-12-08 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my other labs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2181-12-08 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count is normal, no infection. Liver and kidney function are stable. We’ll check your INR and phosphate again before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2181-12-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on full liquids for over 24 hours with no issues. The G-tube has been clamped, and you’re not needing suction. That’s a big improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2181-12-09 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2181-12-09 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if all goes well today, we’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. You’ll stay on full liquids and follow up with your GI doctor before trying solids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2181-12-09 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my meds? Are they changing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2181-12-09 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No major changes. We’re increasing your trazodone to 150 mg at bedtime for sleep. Everything else stays the same, including your warfarin and thyroid meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2181-12-09 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Phenergan for nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2181-12-09 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll keep that as needed, especially before meals. We’re sending home 120 tablets."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2181-12-09 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest INR is 2.8—perfect for warfarin. Phosphate is 5.9, so still a bit high. Keep taking TUMS with Ensure and limit to three bottles a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2181-12-09 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. When do I get the lab work done?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2181-12-09 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have blood drawn three days after discharge to check INR and phosphate. Call your primary doctor with the results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2181-12-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. Vital signs are stable, pain is controlled, and you’ve tolerated full liquids without nausea. We’re ready to discharge you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2181-12-10 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2181-12-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or go to the ER if you have fever, severe abdominal pain, vomiting, or shortness of breath. Otherwise, keep on full liquids and follow up with GI in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2181-12-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my G-tube site? Any signs of infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2181-12-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep it clean and dry. If it becomes red, swollen, or starts draining pus, let us know. Right now, it looks clean and healing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2181-12-10 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2181-12-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2181-12-10 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2181-12-10 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired but much better. Ready to be home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2181-12-10 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Remember: full liquids, TUMS with Ensure, no solids yet, and follow up with GI. We’ll send your discharge papers now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2181-12-10 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly with your prescriptions and instructions. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2181-12-10 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’ve got it all. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2181-12-10 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Take it slow at home and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2181-12-10 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you’ve reviewed the discharge instructions and have all your meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2181-12-10 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, everything’s here. I’ll follow up with my doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2181-12-10 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. You’re cleared to go home. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2181-12-10 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your dizziness has improved, but be careful when standing. Rise slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2181-12-10 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve been doing that the last few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2181-12-10 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Keep up the progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2181-12-10 16:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Transport is here to take you home. We’re glad you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2181-12-10 16:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2181-12-10 16:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2181-12-10 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in one last time. All set to go?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2181-12-10 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, all set. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2181-12-10 17:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2181-12-05 18:12:00",
    "admission_end": "2181-12-10 18:11:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with a history of fibrosing mesenteritis and recurrent partial small bowel obstructions, was admitted for abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and dizziness. Imaging showed persistent unconnected tubing in the small bowel with new wall thickening, likely contributing to functional obstruction. She was managed conservatively with bowel rest, IV fluids, and symptom control. Her G-tube was successfully replaced as planned. She gradually advanced to a full liquid diet, tolerated clamping of the G-tube, and showed improvement in symptoms. She was discharged home in good condition with instructions to continue full liquids, monitor phosphate levels with TUMS when consuming Ensure, and follow up with gastroenterology before advancing to solids.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Dehydration",
      "Irritable bowel syndrome",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Sicca syndrome",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants"
    ]
  }
}
